  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "7978bd68-7f98-430c-b12a-8d547a48110b",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1008,
        2176
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## UGC Ad Video Generator - Photo to Reel\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow turns a submitted product photo into a UGC-style ad reel. It uploads and publishes the image, generates an ad script with DeepSeek, creates a video job with Seedance Mini, then polls until the job succeeds or fails. Successful videos are downloaded, saved to Google Drive, and logged to Google Sheets; failures are marked and logged separately.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the form trigger fields for the UGC ad request, including the product photo and any product details used in the prompt.\n- Connect Google Drive credentials and set the target folders/permissions for the uploaded product photo and generated video.\n- Add API credentials for DeepSeek and the KIE/Seedance Mini video generation endpoint in the HTTP Request nodes.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and configure the success and failure log sheets with matching columns for status, links, errors, and request metadata.\n- Verify the expressions that build the public image URL, extract the generated script, read the video task ID/status, and parse the final video URL.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the ad script prompt, Seedance model parameters, polling delay, Drive folders, and sheet columns to match the brand, video style, and reporting needs."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "33b38670-d18c-416d-bc85-226f4148abf9",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -448,
        2240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 432,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Receive product request\n\nCaptures a new UGC ad request from the form and receives the submitted product photo for processing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
